  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist \"Okafor CRC 2026\" (grp-okafor-crc, 4 members) worked per RBC-QM-02. Four new items arrived at 08:00 about these patients (inbox-a0001 to a0004). I reviewed them before deciding and closed each with links to what I did.\n\n| Patient | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow (72) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0001), patient messaged (comm-t0004) | No qualifying screening. Her only frailty diagnosis (cond-00189) was marked entered in error by Dr. Lin today (comm-00301), so the frailty + advanced illness exclusion doesn't apply, even though she takes donepezil. No hospice/palliative care, nursing home, CRC or colectomy. |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan (52) | Excluded | Hospice episode eoc-00002 was active 2026-06-16 to 2026-08-21 (pancreatic cancer), now finished. The hospice discharge summary that arrived today (doc-00402) confirms it. No order, no contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss (52) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0002), patient messaged (comm-t0005) | The FIT obs-01732 was corrected today: it was collected 2025-12-31, not 2026-01-05, so it's outside the 2026 measurement period. No other screening and no exclusions. |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver (51) | Open gap: FIT kit ordered (sr-t0003), patient messaged (comm-t0006) | The 2024-06-11 sDNA-FIT (obs-01871) is now entered in error. Harbor lab withdrew it as another patient's specimen (doc-00401). The 2025 colonoscopy order sr-00003 was never done, and an order doesn't count. No exclusions. |\n\nFIT order windows run 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31. None of the patients had an active FIT order before. Messages say the kit is on its way and how to complete and return it, and say nothing false about past screening. A note citing RBC-QM-02 is in each chart (doc-t0007 to t0010). The old colonoscopy order sr-00003 for pt-0024 is still open and needs Dr. Okafor's review. I left the other inbox items, which aren't part of this worklist, untouched.",
